Clicks a visible control

Usage: leptoskit device tap [OPTIONS] <--locator-accessibility-id <LOCATOR_ACCESSIBILITY_ID>|--locator-text <LOCATOR_TEXT>|--locator-id <LOCATOR_ID>|--locator-css <LOCATOR_CSS>|--locator-xpath <LOCATOR_XPATH>>

Options:
      --kind <KIND>
          What to drive; inferred from `--device` or `--url` when omitted

          Possible values:
          - ios-simulator: An Apple simulator, selected by UDID
          - ios-device:    A physically connected iPhone or iPad, selected by UDID
          - android:       An Android device or emulator, selected by adb serial
          - macos:         A native app on this Mac, through an Appium Mac2 driver
          - windows:       A native app on this Windows desktop, through an Appium driver
          - linux:         A native app on this Linux desktop, through an Appium driver
          - web:           A website in a real browser

      --device <DEVICE>
          The simulator UDID, device UDID, or adb serial

      --app <APP>
          The app a session launches or attaches to: an installed identity, a path containing a separator, or `desktop` for the whole Windows or Linux screen

      --url <URL>
          The page a web target opens; implies `--kind web`

      --browser <BROWSER>
          The browser a web target uses

          Possible values:
          - chrome:  Chrome through chromedriver
          - firefox: Firefox through geckodriver
          - safari:  Safari through the macOS safaridriver

      --endpoint <ENDPOINT>
          A W3C endpoint instead of the default: the Appium server, or a remote browser driver that is then not spawned locally

      --headful
          Show the browser window; headless is the default

      --locator-accessibility-id <LOCATOR_ACCESSIBILITY_ID>
          Accessibility identifier, `AutomationId`, content description, or on the web `aria-label`/`data-testid`

      --locator-text <LOCATOR_TEXT>
          Visible text or accessible name

      --locator-id <LOCATOR_ID>
          Native resource or HTML element id

      --locator-css <LOCATOR_CSS>
          A CSS selector; web targets only

      --locator-xpath <LOCATOR_XPATH>
          An explicit `XPath` into the native tree or the DOM

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
